    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3394" root="بهت" body-key="b">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَاهِتٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَبْهُوتٌ</span>, in two places. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also act.
part. n. [of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَهَتَهُ</span>; signifying <i>Causing to become
confounded,</i> &amp;c.: and <i>calumniating,</i> &amp;c.:] from
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">البُهْتَانُ</span>: (Mgh:) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُهُوتٌ</span>, as mentioned above, is
held by ISd and MF to be a pl. of this word;
not of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَهُوتٌ</span>, q. v. (TA.)

